1
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:22,980
Summer has come again this year.

2
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:24,940
It's here, it's here, it's here!

3
00:00:24,940 --> 00:00:25,200
Come on!

4
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:28,480
Big water, drink it all up, the juicy one.

5
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:31,260
Water, here comes the water!

6
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:32,700
Big chests, bouncing along.

7
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:34,420
Stuck to the chest, the juicy one.

8
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:35,780
Up and down.

9
00:00:35,780 --> 00:00:37,440
Jiggle jiggle jiggle
jiggle jiggle jiggle jiggle.

10
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:40,780
Summer has come again this year.

11
00:00:40,780 --> 00:00:43,240
It's here, it's here,
it's here, here it comes!

12
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:46,720
Summer has come again this year.

13
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:48,660
It's here, it's here, here it comes!

14
00:00:48,660 --> 00:00:52,260
Big waves, small waves,
tiny little waves, just about that size.

15
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:55,080
Southern breeze, yellowtail.

16
00:00:55,080 --> 00:00:58,380
Big bottoms, small bottoms,
tiny little ones, just about that size.

17
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,720
In the south wind,

18
00:01:07,720 --> 00:01:13,640
In the south wind,

19
00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:21,000
on the shore, on the shore,
on the shore, on the shore,

20
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:31,320
open Katsuki Bridge!

21
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:41,520
It was a lovely wedding, wasn't it?

22
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:43,880
Roppai!

23
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:51,060
Hey, we came all the way to Ginza.

24
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:52,900
Let's see the Katsuki spot and head back.

25
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:54,780
But we're going the wrong way.

26
00:01:54,780 --> 00:01:56,960
What? If you've got a complaint,
it's like this.

27
00:01:56,960 --> 00:01:58,520
Got it.

28
00:01:58,520 --> 00:01:59,960
Yeah, fine.

29
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:03,620
It's Ryo-chan

30
00:02:14,860 --> 00:02:17,200
Ryo-chan, let's get ready too.

31
00:02:18,580 --> 00:02:21,040
Ryo-chan, we've arrived. Wake up.

32
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:23,340
Honestly, you told me to go by myself.

33
00:02:34,460 --> 00:02:35,180
What?

34
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:37,680
There's a man on the bridge.

35
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:40,240
Isn't he a ghost?

36
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:49,300
Where exactly, Reiko-san?

37
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:51,600
I'm sure he was on top of this steel girder.

38
00:02:54,940 --> 00:02:56,240
Are you sure you didn't mistake it?

39
00:02:57,180 --> 00:02:58,420
I definitely saw him.

40
00:03:09,020 --> 00:03:11,760
Well, what a truly lovely wedding that was.

41
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:15,120
And this morning,
I even found a tea stalk standing upright.

42
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:17,240
I'm in such a good mood.

43
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:19,960
I see.

44
00:03:20,460 --> 00:03:21,980
Thank you for going to all that trouble.

45
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:25,580
As I expected, near Katsuki Bridge

46
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:27,820
there were no incidents or accidents,
it seems.

47
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:30,300
Katsuki Bridge.

48
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:30,860
Excuse me?

49
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:34,420
But I wonder why there was
a person in a place like that?

50
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:35,220
Good morning!

51
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:44,780
Senpai, you're lucky. The chief is
in a really good mood this morning.

52
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:46,160
Lucky.

53
00:03:46,940 --> 00:03:48,180
Good morning.

54
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:51,000
I drank a bit too much.

55
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:54,080
Baka-mono! What time do you think it is?!

56
00:03:55,060 --> 00:03:58,200
Please don't yell. My head's pounding.

57
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:01,520
Get over here!
I'll give you a good scolding!

58
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:02,780
I'm not a stray cat!

59
00:04:03,420 --> 00:04:05,660
Hey! Where's this
"good mood" you're talking about?!

60
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:06,840
Hurry up and get over here!

61
00:04:09,100 --> 00:04:12,300
What could've happened?
He was in such a good mood earlier.

62
00:04:19,780 --> 00:04:21,140
Illegal parking

63
00:04:21,140 --> 00:04:22,240
Good morning.

64
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:24,460
It's a Sapporo plate, isn't it.

65
00:04:24,460 --> 00:04:25,220
Yes.

66
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:27,100
Near Katsuki Bridge,

67
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:29,260
it's been illegally parked since last night.

68
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:30,480
Katsuki Bridge?

69
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:31,320
Since last night?

70
00:04:31,460 --> 00:04:31,640
Yes.

71
00:04:31,640 --> 00:04:33,060
A neighbor said

72
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:34,540
a man in white clothes

73
00:04:34,540 --> 00:04:36,920
who was tall got out of it.

74
00:04:36,920 --> 00:04:37,980
White clothes?

75
00:04:38,420 --> 00:04:39,360
Maybe,

76
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:40,160
the one from last night?

77
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:41,640
Hello?

78
00:04:42,300 --> 00:04:45,562
Could you look up the registered owner of a car?
The plates are from Sapporo.

79
00:04:45,612 --> 00:04:48,060
Looks like it's not just
an illegal parking case.

80
00:04:49,260 --> 00:04:50,160
Is it a case?

81
00:04:50,520 --> 00:04:54,200
No, we haven't confirmed yet that
it belongs to last night's man.

82
00:04:54,700 --> 00:04:57,135
Yes. Toyohira Ward, Sapporo City. Yes.

83
00:04:57,185 --> 00:04:59,479
Shiratori.
Shiro as in white bird, and jun as in pure.

84
00:04:59,529 --> 00:05:03,200
Jun Shiratori, got it. Thank you very much.

85
00:05:03,980 --> 00:05:05,680
What's up with Jun Shiratori?

86
00:05:05,940 --> 00:05:06,320
Yeah.

87
00:05:06,620 --> 00:05:07,800
Ow

88
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:09,440
You know him, Pyo-chan?

89
00:05:09,760 --> 00:05:10,040
Yeah.

90
00:05:11,420 --> 00:05:13,540
He's a friend from my middle school days.

91
00:05:13,540 --> 00:05:16,360
Though,
I suppose it was only for a short while.

92
00:05:16,960 --> 00:05:21,800
And then he left his car parked near
Katsuki Bridge and vanished somewhere.

93
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:22,900
Katsuki Bridge?

94
00:05:23,260 --> 00:05:25,700
I see. He came to see the bridge.

95
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:26,760
The bridge?

96
00:05:26,940 --> 00:05:28,960
What's going on, senpai?

97
00:05:28,960 --> 00:05:33,820
Yeah, back when I was a cute
little middle schooler myself.

98
00:05:33,820 --> 00:05:35,140
Hey, Kankichi!

99
00:05:35,140 --> 00:05:35,620
Yes.

100
00:05:35,620 --> 00:05:35,720
Yes!

101
00:05:45,620 --> 00:05:47,240
Great spinning mid-air kick!

102
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:51,340
I'm getting dizzy!

103
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:02,400
Kankichi!
Who told you to do a mid-air spin?!

104
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:03,640
It's a bonus!

105
00:06:05,620 --> 00:06:06,740
Ahahahaha!

106
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:09,560
Kan-chan, that was amazing, the best!

107
00:06:10,980 --> 00:06:12,440
Jun, did you have fun?

108
00:06:12,820 --> 00:06:15,240
Next time I'll show you
an even flashier one, okay?

109
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:16,200
Kankichi!

110
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:17,240
Yes!

111
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:26,400
So Jun went to the Expo Awesome.

112
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:29,580
But it was so crowded,
he couldn't really see much.

113
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:33,220
Apparently he went by bullet train.
Have you ever ridden the Ton-kichi?

114
00:06:33,220 --> 00:06:35,260
I've only ever ridden the Tobu Line.

115
00:06:36,840 --> 00:06:38,060
Would you like some tea?

116
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:39,720
Excuse us for intruding.

117
00:06:41,660 --> 00:06:43,520
Please enjoy it with everyone.

118
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:45,140
Cake again.

119
00:06:45,660 --> 00:06:47,520
Sorry for always troubling you, ma'am.

120
00:06:48,060 --> 00:06:50,840
That's fine.
Please keep being good friends with Jun.

121
00:06:50,840 --> 00:06:51,420
Yes.

122
00:06:51,980 --> 00:06:53,480
Well, make yourselves at home.

123
00:06:55,960 --> 00:07:00,500
Even when we're watching PE, I never get
bored watching Kan-chan and the others.

124
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:02,920
Kankichi's only redeeming quality is his energy,
you know.

125
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:08,200
I'll show you a backflip next time.

126
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:10,980
In return,
show me your answers again during tests.

127
00:07:11,420 --> 00:07:14,600
My eyesight's 2.5,
so I'm perfect for cheating.

128
00:07:20,320 --> 00:07:22,940
Still, what an amazing book.

129
00:07:22,940 --> 00:07:24,320
Did you all read this book?

130
00:07:24,780 --> 00:07:27,480
Anyway, I can lend it to you anytime.

131
00:07:28,320 --> 00:07:31,960
We're not good with thick books like this,
Tonkichi.

132
00:07:31,960 --> 00:07:34,540
Yeah, textbooks are enough.

133
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:38,960
This one looks interesting, I think.

134
00:07:43,460 --> 00:07:44,260
Japan's

135
00:07:44,260 --> 00:07:46,880
It's called "Japanese Bridges."

136
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:49,160
You like this kind of thing.

137
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:53,560
Isn't that Katsuki Bridge?

138
00:07:54,860 --> 00:07:55,620
It really is.

139
00:07:57,580 --> 00:07:58,400
You know about bridges?

140
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:01,180
I know a bit about them.

141
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:05,598
Shirahige, Kototoi, Azuma,
Komagata, Umaya, Kuramae,

142
00:08:05,648 --> 00:08:08,960
Ryogoku, Kiyosu, Eitai, Tsukuda, Kachidoki.

143
00:08:10,160 --> 00:08:11,980
Those are the bridges over the Sumida River.

144
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:12,820
Wow.

145
00:08:13,260 --> 00:08:15,700
We were made to memorize
them in elementary school.

146
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:19,060
My favorite is Kachidoki Bridge.

147
00:08:19,400 --> 00:08:21,840
Because it goes clank-clank when it moves.

148
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:24,740
I'd like to see it once.

149
00:08:25,500 --> 00:08:26,740
You've never seen it?

150
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:29,340
I want to, but it's far away.

151
00:08:31,740 --> 00:08:34,180
It's close. Just past Ginza.

152
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:36,110
They stop all the cars,

153
00:08:36,160 --> 00:08:38,740
and the bridge slowly opens up, you know.

154
00:08:39,580 --> 00:08:42,700
When you look from on top of the bridge,
the road comes at you like a wall.

155
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,420
It's incredibly impressive.

156
00:08:46,620 --> 00:08:48,780
Wow. I'd love to see it with my own eyes.

157
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:51,100
Let's go. To Kachidoki Bridge now.

158
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:52,900
It's about 20 minutes by bike.

159
00:08:54,820 --> 00:08:55,180
Yeah.

160
00:08:57,740 --> 00:08:59,660
Alright, let's go!

161
00:09:10,280 --> 00:09:12,615
Then appeared,

162
00:09:12,665 --> 00:09:14,520
the champion of justice!

163
00:09:27,840 --> 00:09:28,820
We're almost there!

164
00:09:36,160 --> 00:09:37,160
Look, there it is.

165
00:09:40,300 --> 00:09:41,740
That's the bridge that opens.

166
00:09:44,780 --> 00:09:47,000
From around here, the view is perfect.

167
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:50,000
I always buy bread and
eat it while watching.

168
00:09:50,900 --> 00:09:51,620
A ship's coming!

169
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:53,780
Yes, it's opening!

170
00:10:03,620 --> 00:10:04,880
It's not opening.

171
00:10:04,880 --> 00:10:05,940
That's strange.

172
00:10:05,940 --> 00:10:08,160
It always opens around lunchtime, though.

173
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:10,040
What's going on?

174
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:18,520
It's not going to open anymore?

175
00:10:18,520 --> 00:10:20,580
Yesterday's opening was the last one.

176
00:10:20,580 --> 00:10:22,360
Movable bridges like this are...

177
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:27,160
They say it's the age of
land transport from now on.

178
00:10:27,160 --> 00:10:29,740
Shipping by water would
be so much easier, though.

179
00:10:30,300 --> 00:10:31,720
I had no idea.

180
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:35,140
So Kachidoki Bridge won't open anymore?

181
00:10:35,620 --> 00:10:39,080
Once the city hall decides something,
it'll never open again.

182
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:42,140
Being brought to tears by
the currents of the times...

183
00:10:42,140 --> 00:10:45,040
It's always weak folks like us.

184
00:10:56,960 --> 00:10:59,780
Tch, we came all this way to see it.
What a letdown.

185
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:04,520
Jun was really looking forward to it, too.

186
00:11:05,780 --> 00:11:07,400
Don't be so down, Jun.

187
00:11:14,020 --> 00:11:14,800
Next time.

188
00:11:14,800 --> 00:11:15,800
Yes.

189
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:17,240
Shibayama.

190
00:11:17,240 --> 00:11:18,220
Hey.

191
00:11:18,220 --> 00:11:21,500
Shiratori's absent, then.

192
00:11:22,960 --> 00:11:25,120
Sir, what happened to Jun?

193
00:11:26,020 --> 00:11:28,380
Apparently he came down
with a fever and is in bed.

194
00:11:28,920 --> 00:11:32,260
He seemed pretty shaken up about Katsuki Bridge,
so it's no surprise.

195
00:11:33,560 --> 00:11:34,840
Let's stop by on the way back.

196
00:11:35,980 --> 00:11:37,260
Transfer?

197
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:40,500
I'm moving to Hokkaido,
where the air is clean.

198
00:11:41,340 --> 00:11:43,520
Even though I'd finally
become friends with everyone.

199
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:49,120
Even if we're far apart,
we're still friends!

200
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:49,920
Right!

201
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:52,080
Yeah, that's right.

202
00:11:52,900 --> 00:11:53,220
Just

203
00:11:54,180 --> 00:11:55,880
there's only one thing I regret:

204
00:11:56,280 --> 00:11:59,180
never getting to see
the Kachidoki Bridge open.

205
00:11:59,820 --> 00:12:01,540
I wish we could have
all watched it together.

206
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:04,560
Jun, when are you going to Hokkaido?

207
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:06,700
The day after tomorrow.

208
00:12:07,440 --> 00:12:08,520
That soon?

209
00:12:14,820 --> 00:12:17,960
So Jun-kun is moving away. That's a shame.

210
00:12:18,540 --> 00:12:21,380
We'll never get to eat
cake that delicious again.

211
00:12:22,020 --> 00:12:24,620
Kanchi's test scores will
drop back to zero again.

212
00:12:34,100 --> 00:12:37,820
Jun-kun was really disappointed about the Kachidoki Bridge,
wasn't he?

213
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:40,520
I wish we could have shown him it opening.

214
00:12:41,980 --> 00:12:42,320
That's it!

215
00:12:44,020 --> 00:12:46,140
Let's show him the bridge opening.

216
00:12:47,660 --> 00:12:49,200
So it's impossible now.

217
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:52,320
We'll open it ourselves.

218
00:12:52,700 --> 00:12:55,760
We'll open the bridge
ourselves and show it to Jun.

219
00:13:13,140 --> 00:13:14,400
Kan-chan

220
00:13:18,660 --> 00:13:19,380
Ugh

221
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:23,820
What are you doing up there?

222
00:13:23,820 --> 00:13:27,440
Come on,
I'll show you the Kachidoki Bridge opening.

223
00:13:27,440 --> 00:13:29,360
Wait, the Kachidoki Bridge opens?

224
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:31,100
Yeah, hurry, hurry.

225
00:13:31,780 --> 00:13:33,520
Wait, I'll go change now.

226
00:13:38,080 --> 00:13:39,140
This way, this way.

227
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:44,080
Jun, I'll be right back.

228
00:13:50,060 --> 00:13:57,060
This is still the best view, after all.

229
00:13:57,740 --> 00:13:59,360
Jun-kun, wait here.

230
00:14:00,340 --> 00:14:02,080
Can they really get it to open?

231
00:14:04,020 --> 00:14:05,060
Leave it to us.

232
00:14:05,580 --> 00:14:06,140
Alright, let's go.

233
00:14:18,060 --> 00:14:20,960
Kachidoki Bridge has four towers.

234
00:14:23,940 --> 00:14:26,780
Of those, only that one has stairs.

235
00:14:26,780 --> 00:14:28,720
That must be the control room.

236
00:14:29,540 --> 00:14:30,780
I'll raise the bridge.

237
00:14:30,780 --> 00:14:32,620
You two stop the cars.

238
00:14:33,060 --> 00:14:33,460
Got it.

239
00:14:41,200 --> 00:14:42,900
Just as I thought, it's here.

240
00:14:44,640 --> 00:14:46,300
Sure enough, it's locked.

241
00:14:47,440 --> 00:14:48,920
But that's useless.

242
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:52,280
Opening locks is my specialty.

243
00:14:52,280 --> 00:14:53,600
Stop!

244
00:14:54,460 --> 00:14:55,960
Please stop!

245
00:14:55,960 --> 00:14:57,220
Hurry up!

246
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,520
No good, it won't stop at all!

247
00:15:04,020 --> 00:15:05,020
This one's no good either!

248
00:15:07,220 --> 00:15:07,820
It opened!

249
00:15:08,880 --> 00:15:09,720
Clank clank!

250
00:15:16,680 --> 00:15:18,100
So many switches!

251
00:15:22,540 --> 00:15:24,740
Guess it won't move unless we cut the power.

252
00:15:25,540 --> 00:15:26,980
How do we make this thing work?

253
00:15:27,660 --> 00:15:28,800
Stop!

254
00:15:29,380 --> 00:15:30,000
Please!

255
00:15:30,560 --> 00:15:31,320
Stop!

256
00:15:31,620 --> 00:15:32,840
The legs are opening!

257
00:15:35,360 --> 00:15:35,900
Stop!

258
00:15:38,440 --> 00:15:39,740
Yes! It stopped!

259
00:15:45,500 --> 00:15:47,600
Hey, what do you think you're doing?

260
00:15:48,940 --> 00:15:51,020
What are you planning,
stopping cars like that?

261
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:53,700
Hey!

262
00:15:58,680 --> 00:16:00,520
Taxi! The cop spotted us!

263
00:16:02,380 --> 00:16:04,520
Hey, get back here!

264
00:16:14,440 --> 00:16:16,400
Taxi, close the door!

265
00:16:20,400 --> 00:16:21,520
Hey, open up!

266
00:16:22,100 --> 00:16:22,940
What do you think you're doing?

267
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:26,880
This isn't working. The cars won't stop,
and now the cops have spotted us.

268
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:29,620
The plan was a little too reckless.
Let's call it off.

269
00:16:30,520 --> 00:16:32,740
Jun's waiting for us, you know!

270
00:16:34,180 --> 00:16:35,900
Will it really open?

271
00:16:37,820 --> 00:16:42,360
But how are we supposed to raise it?
Let's just give up.

272
00:16:43,700 --> 00:16:48,380
Open the door! Come out of there right now.
What do you plan to do?

273
00:16:49,620 --> 00:16:53,100
We're still going to raise the bridge.
Now is our only chance.

274
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:57,200
Alright, screw it, we're going all in.

275
00:16:57,860 --> 00:16:58,820
The power...

276
00:17:00,360 --> 00:17:01,160
Don't touch it!

277
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:09,320
The power's on!

278
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:11,520
Okay, turn on all the switches!

279
00:17:13,700 --> 00:17:15,280
Stop the cars right now!

280
00:17:16,300 --> 00:17:16,800
Stop it!

281
00:17:16,800 --> 00:17:18,080
Open up!

282
00:17:20,780 --> 00:17:22,880
The Kachidoki Bridge signal's on!

283
00:17:23,100 --> 00:17:26,100
No way!
That bridge was supposed to be closed!

284
00:17:28,860 --> 00:17:31,320
Move! The bridge is going up!

285
00:17:39,480 --> 00:17:41,680
Please, just move! Kachidoki Bridge!

286
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:42,960
Stop!

287
00:17:46,540 --> 00:17:47,880
Don't come in! This place is dangerous!

288
00:17:48,680 --> 00:17:50,820
Kachidoki Bridge! Open up!

289
00:17:56,100 --> 00:17:59,100
Aaaaaah!

290
00:17:59,960 --> 00:18:05,060
Aaaaaah!

291
00:18:16,860 --> 00:18:18,580
Aaaaaah!

292
00:18:18,580 --> 00:18:19,720
Aaaaaah!

293
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:20,740
Aaaaaah!

294
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:36,300
Open, open!

295
00:18:36,300 --> 00:18:37,780
Keep opening!

296
00:18:37,780 --> 00:18:39,580
Open wider, wider!

297
00:18:44,180 --> 00:18:47,740
So the bridge really does open after all!

298
00:18:57,800 --> 00:19:18,820
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

299
00:19:32,280 --> 00:19:34,160
Yay! It's fully open!

300
00:19:34,700 --> 00:19:35,640
Yay!

301
00:19:36,540 --> 00:19:38,120
The Kachidoki Bridge opened!

302
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:40,100
It's like it's doing a banzai!

303
00:19:40,860 --> 00:19:42,340
The bridge opened again?

304
00:19:42,920 --> 00:19:45,520
The Kachidoki Bridge really
should be like that, right?

305
00:19:46,580 --> 00:19:48,300
Sumida's face is like that, after all.

306
00:19:49,140 --> 00:19:50,120
It's really amazing.

307
00:19:52,560 --> 00:19:54,700
It's beyond imagination, Kan-chan.

308
00:19:58,740 --> 00:19:59,940
We did it, we did it!

309
00:20:01,020 --> 00:20:02,660
I wonder if Jun was watching?

310
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:18,560
Ha-ha! You'd better be ready,
I'm going to arrest every last one of you!

311
00:20:19,120 --> 00:20:21,360
No good, we can't escape like this!

312
00:20:21,360 --> 00:20:22,040
What do we do?

313
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:24,680
Come on!

314
00:20:25,580 --> 00:20:26,580
What are you doing?

315
00:20:26,580 --> 00:20:27,300
Bye-bye!

316
00:20:34,540 --> 00:20:37,140
Hey, we're running off
and leaving the bridge up!

317
00:20:37,700 --> 00:20:41,380
Honestly, what a bunch of troublemakers!

318
00:20:42,380 --> 00:20:46,540
Help! Help!

319
00:20:57,380 --> 00:20:58,500
Run away!

320
00:21:07,220 --> 00:21:11,460
Then he swam all the way to Hamarikyu,
then came back again

321
00:21:11,460 --> 00:21:15,120
and watched the Kachidoki
Bridge fuss from a safe perch.

322
00:21:16,760 --> 00:21:18,780
He was always the daring type, wasn't he?

323
00:21:18,780 --> 00:21:21,560
He must have been overjoyed, Jun-kun.

324
00:21:21,560 --> 00:21:22,745
He certainly was.

325
00:21:22,795 --> 00:21:25,620
I can't forget that excited smile of his.

326
00:21:25,620 --> 00:21:31,440
But if that Jun abandoned his car and
climbed up our memorable Kachidoki Bridge,

327
00:21:31,440 --> 00:21:32,760
maybe...

328
00:21:34,620 --> 00:21:35,980
That's absolutely impossible.

329
00:21:35,980 --> 00:21:39,240
He was physically weak,
but his heart was strong.

330
00:21:39,240 --> 00:21:40,240
Excuse me.

331
00:21:42,320 --> 00:21:43,540
The car out front...

332
00:21:44,280 --> 00:21:45,120
Jun...

333
00:21:47,720 --> 00:21:48,920
Kan-chan

334
00:21:48,920 --> 00:21:51,140
What are you doing here?

335
00:21:51,140 --> 00:21:53,480
Believe it or not, I'm a police officer.

336
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:55,280
Kan-chan became a police officer?

337
00:21:57,020 --> 00:21:59,240
Don't laugh,
you're the one with an illegally parked car.

338
00:22:00,200 --> 00:22:00,539
Well,

339
00:22:00,589 --> 00:22:04,740
It broke down, and I just assumed the
repair shop would come and tow it away.

340
00:22:05,200 --> 00:22:07,360
Right, this.

341
00:22:09,200 --> 00:22:12,760
A university professor?
You've really made it, Jun.

342
00:22:13,180 --> 00:22:14,580
It's all thanks to you, Kan-chan.

343
00:22:15,480 --> 00:22:16,081
Back then,

344
00:22:16,131 --> 00:22:20,200
I've never forgotten the thrill of the day
you risked your lives to raise the bridge.

345
00:22:20,560 --> 00:22:22,480
Now I design bridges.

346
00:22:23,240 --> 00:22:25,600
So it was you climbing the Kachidoki Bridge?

347
00:22:26,320 --> 00:22:28,740
There was a part I really wanted to check,
wasn't there.

348
00:22:29,320 --> 00:22:31,660
The Kachidoki Bridge really is impressive,
isn't it.

349
00:22:33,240 --> 00:22:34,100
Chief.

350
00:22:34,100 --> 00:22:36,740
That friend of mine who's
a doctor of engineering,

351
00:22:36,740 --> 00:22:40,080
we all heard it, Ryotsu-kun.

352
00:22:40,080 --> 00:22:42,120
What? You were listening?

353
00:22:42,580 --> 00:22:44,780
Chief, you're definitely acting strange.

354
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:45,360
Yeah.

355
00:22:45,360 --> 00:22:47,900
Didn't you say that when the bridge went up,

356
00:22:47,900 --> 00:22:50,860
a police officer was dangling from it too?

357
00:22:50,860 --> 00:22:52,320
That's right.

358
00:22:52,480 --> 00:22:57,620
Even now, it's a riot to remember. He kicked his
legs frantically and struggled with everything he had,

359
00:22:57,620 --> 00:23:00,440
but in the end,
he splashed into the river, plop!

360
00:23:02,740 --> 00:23:06,140
Do you remember that officer's face?

361
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:10,140
Of course. With these sinister eyes,

362
00:23:10,140 --> 00:23:13,960
thick eyebrows,
and a long, droopy upper lip,

363
00:23:13,960 --> 00:23:18,360
and on top of that, a mouth like a tightly clamped purse.
There's no way to forget that, no matter how hard you try.

364
00:23:18,360 --> 00:23:19,200
Ryo-chan.

365
00:23:20,080 --> 00:23:21,400
The Chief's face.

366
00:23:22,480 --> 00:23:23,200
What about his face?

367
00:23:23,420 --> 00:23:27,000
A purse mouth, a long upper lip,
narrow eyes, thick...

368
00:23:27,480 --> 00:23:28,420
N-no way...

369
00:23:34,980 --> 00:23:37,140
I'm that police officer!

370
00:23:37,140 --> 00:23:42,260
Gahh!

371
00:23:44,200 --> 00:23:46,190
Hmph, hmph, hmph, hmph, hmph,

372
00:23:46,240 --> 00:23:50,320
So I've finally found the culprit
behind that whole commotion.

373
00:23:50,400 --> 00:23:52,080
Now, calm down, Chief!

374
00:23:52,640 --> 00:23:55,580
Grr, hey, wait!

375
00:23:56,480 --> 00:23:58,140
It's already past the
statute of limitations!

376
00:24:04,040 --> 00:24:06,800
Yes! We won the cheap
seats for the grand sumo!

377
00:24:06,800 --> 00:24:08,640
Those seats fit four people,

378
00:24:08,640 --> 00:24:11,200
so I'll invite Reiko and
bring Nakagawa along too.

379
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:13,400
Now, who should I take for the last seat?

380
00:24:13,400 --> 00:24:15,680
Chief, I was just joking!

381
00:24:15,680 --> 00:24:17,520
I'm inviting you too, Chief, honestly!

382
00:24:17,520 --> 00:24:20,860
Let's really enjoy the grand sumo next time,
alright?

383
00:24:32,280 --> 00:24:36,700
Let's always smile, okay?

384
00:24:36,700 --> 00:24:40,900
Even when something outrageous happens,

385
00:24:40,900 --> 00:24:45,420
keep smiling sweetly, okay?

386
00:24:45,420 --> 00:24:50,640
just step out with a carefree face,
that's all.

387
00:24:50,640 --> 00:24:54,160
Hey, smile for me, won't you?

388
00:24:54,160 --> 00:24:57,600
It's not your fault.

389
00:24:58,860 --> 00:25:02,840
Hey, smile for me, won't you?

390
00:25:02,840 --> 00:25:05,780
Keep up the same spirit as before.

391
00:25:05,780 --> 00:25:11,620
Keep smiling all the time, okay?

392
00:25:11,620 --> 00:25:16,600
Women who act all serious aren't beautiful,

393
00:25:16,600 --> 00:25:21,400
so you should start smiling right away.

394
00:25:21,400 --> 00:25:25,960
Hey, if you're not a child,

